<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd">
<topic id="icons">
  <title>Icons</title>
  <shortdesc>When enabled, DITA Bootstrap includes Bootstrap Icons by default. Additional icon libraries such as
    <xref href="https://fontawesome.com/" format="html" scope="external">Font Awesome</xref>
    <xref href="https://feathericons.com/" format="html" scope="external">Feather</xref> and
    <xref href="https://octicons.github.com/" format="html" scope="external">Octicons</xref> can also be added using
    command line parameters.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Icons</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>style</xmlatt></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>othermeta</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section>
      <title>Bootstrap Icons</title>
      <p>
        <xref href="https://icons.getbootstrap.com/" format="html" scope="external">Bootstrap Icons</xref> is a growing
        library of SVG icons that are designed by @mdo and maintained by the Bootstrap Team. They are open source and
        licensed under MIT, just like Bootstrap so the icon set is freely available to everyone. A <xmlelement
        >Link</xmlelement> to the default Bootstrap Icons CDN set is included by default. </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <title>Example</title>
      <p>Icon fonts with classes for every icon are included in Bootstrap Icons. Include the icon web fonts in your page
        via CSS, then reference the class names as needed in your DITA (e.g., <xmlelement>icon
          outputclass="bi-alarm"/</xmlelement>).</p>
      <p>Use a <xmlatt>style</xmlatt> attribute and alter the CSS font-size and color to change the icon
        appearance.</p>
    </section>
    <fig>
      <title>Icons</title>
      <image href="src/icons/example.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/icons/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/icons/example.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
  <p>Icons placed within an <xmlelement>xref</xmlelement> element are colorized appropriately:</p>
  <fig>
    <title>Links with Icons</title>
    <image href="src/icons/dark-link.png" scalefit="yes"/>
  </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/icons/dark-link.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/icons/dark-link.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <p>Icons can also be placed within buttons as shown:</p>
    <fig>
      <title>Buttons with Icons</title>
      <image href="src/icons/icons-in-buttons.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/icons/icons-in-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/icons/icons-in-buttons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
  </body>
</topic>
